<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ballon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">845</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ballon was fought on 22 November 845 near Bains-sur-Oust in eastern Brittany, between the Breton ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe">Nominoe</a> and the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bretons">Bretons</a> defeated the Frankish army, and Charles was forced to accept Nominoe's authority in Brittany, a key step towards an independent Breton kingdom.</p></div>
